Shoulder pain — begin with the question, not a diagnosis (@shoulder-pain: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @shoulder, #source @med-source-aaos-overview, #source @med-source-msd-shoulder, #medicine @shoulder-rotation-pain, #orthopedics @shoulder-rotation-pain, #shoulder @shoulder-rotation-pain, #medicine @shoulder-stiffness, #orthopedics @shoulder-stiffness, #shoulder @shoulder-stiffness, #medicine @shoulder-instability, #orthopedics @shoulder-instability, #shoulder @shoulder-instability, #medicine @shoulder-referred, #orthopedics @shoulder-referred, #shoulder @shoulder-referred) { r_6NFPQQ7Z2DAF090E4JVN6MQ0FR
**Read a complete clinical introduction:** [Shoulder pain and common problems — AAOS](../../../sources/Shoulder-problems-AAOS.lingua#r_506TD94GKTCRNS0XP0W5Q7EWDV), including the history and examination discussion. Then read Exame do ombro and Distúrbios do ombro in [Avaliação do ombro — Manual MSD](../../../sources/Avaliacao-do-ombro-MSD.lingua#r_51H0EB6JRBDW2X2HNEBY52FG6X), using the normal anatomy to interpret its terms. [Pain near the end of rotation — understand the possibilities](Pain-near-end-of-rotation.lingua#r_34B2Q55P8Q42JP4DWNE7VQTMT6) will narrow this broad account to a positional complaint.

Describe onset, trauma, location, course, stiffness, perceived weakness, altered sensation, relevant activities, and effects on daily life. Pain felt over the lateral upper arm is not a direct drawing of which structure is involved. More than one finding can be present.

The next readings compare cuff-related complaints, calcific tendinopathy, biceps and labrum problems, stiffness, instability, AC and SC disorders, fractures, arthritis, and neurological or systemic causes. Their overlapping descriptions explain why history and examination matter.

Active movement is produced by the person's muscles; passive movement is produced by an examiner moving the region. A difference between them can inform assessment but does not establish one diagnosis. Pain-limited effort and reduced strength also need to be distinguished.

**Try:** write two plausible explanations for a fictional report of difficulty reaching overhead. For each, state what information is missing. Use the safety and care links in [Medicine — understanding the body and its care](../../../Medicine.lingua#r_6DTDCDP6JQ2AV7S78QPGKM2V65) for urgent symptoms; do not attempt to confirm a diagnosis by repeatedly provoking pain.

**Continue:** [Pain near the end of rotation — understand the possibilities](Pain-near-end-of-rotation.lingua#r_34B2Q55P8Q42JP4DWNE7VQTMT6) · [A stiff shoulder — capsulitis and other explanations](Stiff-shoulder.lingua#r_4JWG5NRDXS1ZHGKN05W8J3TAH2) · [Instability, subluxation, and dislocation](Instability.lingua#r_4ANS5B79S566BS78A7E9H5X8R6) · [Nerve disorders and pain referred to the shoulder](Nerve-and-referred-pain.lingua#r_7BFZ7QKTEBQWTCQD9A60VXWDH5).

